<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec nickel imports down 25.1 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec nickel imports down 25.1 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined nickel imports fell 25.1 percent to 3,278 tonnes in December from 4,379 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (on a customs-cleared basis, in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Dec 96	 Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p> Total	   3,278	  4,376	 4,379</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Russia	    814	    401	 1,778</p>
<p> S. Africa	  20	     60	   256</p>
<p> Zimbabwe	  197	    657	   430</p>
<p>Imports in 1996 totalled 53,852 tonnes, down 23.2 percent from 70,128 tonnes in the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
